 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T17:06:20.106288Z",
 "text": "**Not enforceable.** Under the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 (Ontario), a landlord cannot charge a late fee for rent paid after the due date. Section 133 prohibits a landlord from collecting a late payment charge of this kind, so the $50 charge cannot be imposed under the lease. Any tenancy agreement term that conflicts with the Act is also of no effect, since the Act applies despite contrary terms in the lease.\n\nA tenant who has been charged a late fee can apply to the Landlord and Tenant Board. I've identified section 133 from memory, so please confirm the exact wording against the current consolidated Act on e-Laws before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 133",
